+# shader
+
+## change [Split table calls]
+
+- [Split table calls](../../../core/shader/recompiler/ControlFlow/src/GraphBuilder.cpp) - with `APS5_SPLIT_TABLE_CALLS`, a compute table call in a waterfall loop runs as an entry part, one part per callee and a resume part, in slices whose saved state fits in `APS5_SPLIT_STATE_BYTES`, with compute barriers between parts that the console does not have. An indirect dispatch runs `APS5_SPLIT_SLICES` slices, so its groups past them are not run. Not handled: a callee that writes a register the loop reads (the replay runs the loop without the other callees, so its picks can differ), and code after the loop that reads a scalar register a callee wrote (it sees the value from before the loop). Goto variables are not saved. Each part's loops stop with a reported fault after 2^12 iterations per entry, so a longer console loop is cut short. A part whose LDS or scratch is in device memory, or whose state exceeds `maxStorageBufferRange`, throws. Split dispatches use no recipes and no dispatch cache.
+
+## add Functional
+
+- [Loop guard](../../../core/shader/recompiler/SpirvBackend/src/SpirvFlowEmitter.cpp) (shader recompiler) - with `APS5_LOOP_GUARD=<iterations>`, each structured loop counts its back edges in a variable cleared when the loop is entered, and its conditional exits leave once the count reaches the limit; every other loop of the invocation then leaves at its next conditional exit, and one `LoopLimit` fault is recorded when the invocation returns. A console loop that legitimately runs longer is cut short, and the loops after it compute different results (the fault is reported). A loop whose exits are all unconditional branches inside a conditional part of its body has no exit the guard can force, and is not stopped. The cost per iteration (a counter increment, two loads and a compare at each exit) was not measured on hardware.
